   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6Y86",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "Christchurch is experiencing a resurgence, powered by the creativity and determination of our communities. I'm running because I believe good leadership can help unlock what comes next. Imagine what our city could achieve with an MP who fights for Christchurch every day and puts people at the centre of decisions. I want everyone to afford a warm home, put food on the table, access great public services and live in a thriving, climate-safe city."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6YA1",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I'm a mum, community advocate and MP who believes politics should be about showing up, listening and getting things done. In Parliament I've fought for disabled people and whānau, children, artists, safer drug laws and a fairer, greener Aotearoa. I build relationships across communities and political lines, but I never lose sight of who I'm there for. Christchurch deserves an energetic local champion who will fight for it every single day."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6YBw",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Make homes and food affordable: build enough housing and ensure no one goes hungry."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6YDr",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Make public transport cheaper and more reliable. Invest in a system that works for Christchurch."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6YFm",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Make tax fair: tax the super-rich to cut tax for 96% of New Zealanders and fund public services."
     }
    ],
