   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6YX3",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "To provide a campaign full of unique and excellent policies you can't get from anywhere else. Because in order to truly fix this country's issues, an outsider's mindset is needed. A framework devoid of corporate slogans and fake promises. It is my belief that running in Christchurch Central will further expose the electorate to wonderful policies such as cutting GST to 10% and universal dental care."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6YYy",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I've lived in Christchurch my entire life and bring a real sense of kitchen table politics. I'm not going to lecture people on what they can say, smoke or think. Instead I would prioritise investment into healthcare, ending the war on drugs and much more. I'm particularly passionate about electoral reform/systems which I've been studying for several years at this point, in the ambitious endeavour of one day implementing \"spare voting\" in New Zealand."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6Yat",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Cutting GST to 10%. It's a regressive tax that harms the poor and increases prices simultaneously."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6Yco",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Implementing free public transport + free dental. Can be paid for by increased taxes on the wealthy."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6Yej",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Restoring the $1.8 billion in transport funding that was meant to go to the South Island."
     }
    ],
